WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.229
The lab runs in a test
tenant, never production,

2
00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:06.325
and the authors haven't
run it, as the page says.

3
00:00:06.325 --> 00:00:10.362
There's no fixture lab in this path,
because the guide has no kit yet.

4
00:00:10.362 --> 00:00:13.988
You need a test tenant with
Global Secure Access onboarded,

5
00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:18.650
an administrator with the Global Secure
Access Administrator or Security

6
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:23.237
Administrator role activated through
pim, Graph PowerShell, and Azure C L I.

7
00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:26.863
Steps one and two make a lab
folder, connect with read scopes,

8
00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:30.488
and export the licenses and
the tenant's onboarding status.

9
00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:34.550
Compare the licenses by product name
with Learn's licensing section.

10
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.424
Step three takes the baseline
export: nine Graph requests,

11
00:00:39.424 --> 00:00:44.400
each written to a file, then a S
H A two fifty-six hash manifest.

12
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.750
The slide abbreviates; the module
page has every command in full.

13
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.401
The guide's Validate: the tenant shows
onboarded, the license count covers

14
00:00:53.401 --> 00:00:58.030
the pilot and the first ring, and the
export folder and its manifest exist.
